free_refresh.py` / ADR 0055 beyond the already-landed docstring-citation history.\nStep 0(c): fresh worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/fix-3e03-adr-cite` is current at origin/main 024a6a2278134128be0c76c8d7c60e41b4ba817d.\n\nProven root cause: the f449-era narrative cited the pre-renumbering/non-current ADR number for Jira DC search-index lag. Current `docs/adr/0037-oss-contribution-intake-posture.md` is the GitHub PR / OSS contribution posture ADR, while `docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md` §3 states that Jira's search index lags create/delete by an unbounded interval, and `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` line ~282 records the Jira-family sub-seam's `Search-index lag` edge. Static discriminating evidence: `git show 3b92fad7df3c:src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` shows the original docstring line `unbounded — ADR 0037 s3`; the current f449 description still had `background reindex is UNBOUNDED (ADR 0037 s3)`. Reading ADR 0037 vs ADR 0085/0055 proves the cited target, not the reindex behavior, was wrong.\n\nDefect legitimacy: defect / plan documentation error. The authoritative ADR files establish the correct targets; the f449 description sent readers to an unrelated ADR.\n\nDefect origin: f449-be6a-be56-4fef (seagreen-fortuitous-crayfish). Commit 3b92fad7df3c (`Refresh scoped keys before diff (bug f449)`) introduced the original module docstring with `ADR 0037 s3`, and the f449 ticket description carried the same stale citation. Later ticket 79a4 partially corrected the docstring to ADR 0055, but the f449 ticket description remained stale and the docstring still needed the current unbounded-lag ADR 0085 citation. I will close 3e03 with `--caused-by=f449-be6a-be56-4fef`.\n\nNo behavioral RED test is warranted: this is citation/docstring/tracker text only, with no runtime behavior. The oracle is static inspection/grep plus the project verification suite.","timestamp":1788324909126605225}],"created_at":1788288573500695001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ad1a39f3-cd9c-4406-b3b8-e34eb1b69c2d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f449-be6a-be56-4fef"},{"link_uuid":"4a57ec75-b3bb-4d4b-b3a6-4f94e7956041","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"6efaa5de-7128-45b4-a4c0-b2e4b656bc30","provenance":"explicit","relation":"caused_by","target_id":"f449-be6a-be56-4fef"},{"link_uuid":"5c63aaea-1021-4b4e-bceb-6f556bdf883f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"052f-736d-72a3-4f8c"}],"description":"# Fix f449 ADR citation for unbounded Jira DC reindex support\n\n## Problem\nThe f449 ticket description still cites \"ADR 0037 s3\" for the unbounded Jira DC reindex behavior, but ADR 0037 is now `oss-contribution-intake-posture`. The renumbered ADR that owns the **unbounded** Jira search-index-lag rule is `docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md` §3 (\"Eventual-consistency discipline for live probes\"). The Jira-family sub-seam context for DC search-index lag is also recorded in `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md`, in the \"Search-index lag\" row around line 282.\n\nThe current `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` module docstring already cites ADR 0055 rather than ADR 0037; this ticket will make that docstring citation explicit and consistent by naming `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` / the \"Search-index lag\" row, and by citing ADR 0085 §3 only for the unbounded-index-lag claim.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope for this ticket:\n- the f449 ticket description text (`f449-be6a-be56-4fef`, alias `seagreen-fortuitous-crayfish`);\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` module docstring only;\n- `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` only if the ADR wording itself needs consistency (expected read-only).\n\nOut of scope: other ADR 0037 references in live-harness/test documentation. A repo-wide grep will be reported so non-f449 stale references are visible, but this bug's fix is limited to the f449-era description/docstring citation.\n\n## Verification plan\n- Inspect `docs/adr/0037-oss-contribution-intake-posture.md` to confirm ADR 0037 is the GitHub PR / OSS contribution posture ADR, not Jira DC reindex support.\n- Inspect `docs/adr/0085-reconciler-live-validation-harness.md` §3 to confirm the unbounded search-index-lag statement.\n- Inspect `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` around the \"Search-index lag\" row to confirm the Jira-family sub-seam citation target.\n- Run `grep -nE '\\bADR 0037\\b|0037 s3|oss-contribution-intake-posture|\\bADR 0055\\b|0055-jira-family-sub-seam|\\bADR 0085\\b' src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` and inspect the f449 description to prove the in-scope stale citation is gone and the replacement citation points to ADR 0055 / ADR 0085 according to each ADR's actual title and section content.\n- Run `grep -rnE '\\bADR 0037\\b|0037 s3' . | grep -iE 'reindex|Jira DC|Lucene|unbounded'` and record the hits, classifying each as in-scope (fixed here) or out-of-scope (reported).\n- Run the project verification commands (`make lint && make typecheck && make test`) after the docstring-only code change.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The f449 ticket description no longer points readers to ADR 0037 / `oss-contribution-intake-posture` for Jira DC reindex behavior; it points the unbounded-index-lag claim to ADR 0085 §3 and the Jira-family search-index-lag context to ADR 0055 / `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` instead.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py` cites `docs/adr/0055-jira-family-sub-seam.md` or ADR 0055 for the Jira-family sub-seam/search-index-lag support, cites ADR 0085 §3 only for the unbounded search-index-lag rule if it uses that claim, and contains no `ADR 0037` / `0037 s3` Jira-DC-reindex citation.\n- [ ] A repo-wide grep for `ADR 0037` / `0037 s3` near `reindex`, `Jira DC`, `Lucene`, or `unbounded` is recorded, with in-scope hits fixed here and any out-of-scope hits explicitly reported.\n- [ ] Project verification is green with the worktree virtualenv first on `PATH`.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/snapshot_lagfree_refresh.py","reason":"Correct stale module-docstring ADR citation for Jira DC reindex support."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","052f-736d-72a3-4f8c"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4c4ac961-8f24-4fad-8122-26c97c078070","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3e03-786b-cdc7-460b","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Fix f449 ADR citation for unbounded Jira DC reindex support","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9554fb01-8890-4463-8d7a-b11300a462e1","4b17119c-17de-4eb3-b831-1a446cfcb4f3","a8c09553-fee6-44d3-82c8-4d983a13a885","4a57ec75-b3bb-4d4b-b3a6-4f94e7956041","983a07d3-d0af-4854-8e45-9258bc6d6550","45cbc4f4-9978-48b0-abac-0b355bb81f18","4c4ac961-8f24-4fad-8122-26c97c078070","05cc323e-419f-452e-8fc1-9dc4269f808e","18afb1a5-6618-4437-b64d-84f93316b00b","6efaa5de-7128-45b4-a4c0-b2e4b656bc30","5c63aaea-1021-4b4e-bceb-6f556bdf883f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788330728623711393,"uuid":"3a4033f0-beba-483e-8929-f6d31e9f8964"}